title: Anything triggers anything
intro: Components name what they do, and a Trigger does it when a message arrives. No code, and it works with every part of Griff.
project: Platformer | Triggers

chapter: The flag pulls the lever | A Trigger on the lever
select: Checkpoint
set: Checkpoint.Message = Reached
say: The checkpoint flag already sends a message when the player reaches it. Call it Reached.
select: Lever
look: -6, 0, 7
add: Trigger
explain: component:Trigger | Trigger | Any entity can have a Trigger, one for each thing it reacts to. When its message arrives, it does something.
pick: Trigger.Message = Reached
pick: Trigger.Do = On
explain: field:Trigger.Do | Do | What it can do is a list of what its targets can do. With no targets it's this lever, so: switch on, off or toggle, or set a flag.
expectvalue: Lever.Trigger.Do = On
say: Every component names its actions this way: doors open and lock, spawners spawn, shooters fire, health takes damage, turn orders end the turn, boards pause and restart. A script's own methods join in with one attribute.

chapter: Driving something else | Targets, a value, and who it hears
create: Empty
rename: Rules
add: Trigger
pick: Trigger.Message = Reached
pick: Trigger.Targets = Slime
pick: Trigger.Do = Damage
set: Trigger.With = 2
expectvalue: Rules.Trigger.Do = Damage
explain: field:Trigger.With | With | Damage takes an amount, so the trigger says how much. Two hits is all the slime has.
pick: Trigger.From = Checkpoint
say: And From means it only listens to the checkpoint, so two things sending the same message can be told apart.
look: -4, 0, 9
expectlink: Rules > Slime = Reached: Damage 2
explain: link:Rules > Slime | Reached: Damage 2 | The Scene view draws a line from the trigger to what it drives, saying what it does there.
expectlink: Checkpoint > Rules = Reached
explain: link:Checkpoint > Rules | Reached | And one from what it listens to.

chapter: Playing it | Run to the flag
play
hold: Right 1.4
waitfor: Bridge | 5
waitgone: Slime | 5
explain: game | The flag | Reaching the flag pulled the lever, so the bridge came out, and it struck down the slime on the ledge. A pickup could fire a cannon, a match could end the turn, a beat could open a door: anything can trigger anything.
stop
